From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] exo: a client's overlay priority hint must not crash Ash

Exo still offers the overlay_prioritizer protocol, which only Lacros used
to send hints over. Every Chromium-based Wayland client (Electron apps such
as Obsidian or balenaEtcher, Chrome for Linux on Wayland) finds it and sets
a hint on its surfaces. Surface::AppendContentsToFrame then hit
CHECK_EQ(REGULAR, overlay_priority_hint) and the browser process died with
the whole session as soon as such a window was drawn.

On ChromeOS such apps reach Exo through sommelier, which does not pass the
protocol on, so this never showed. NickelOS apps talk to Exo directly. The
hint keeps steering dmabuf feedback as before; drawing ignores it, as it did
when the CHECK held.

diff --git a/components/exo/surface.cc b/components/exo/surface.cc
index d713008b177b1..108e71e9133c8 100644
--- a/components/exo/surface.cc
+++ b/components/exo/surface.cc
@@ -1762,7 +1762,9 @@ void Surface::AppendContentsToFrame(const gfx::PointF& parent_to_root_px,
         texture_quad->set_force_rgbx();
       }
 
-      CHECK_EQ(exo::OverlayPriority::REGULAR, state_.overlay_priority_hint);
+      // Clients may set a priority hint through overlay_prioritizer (every
+      // Chromium-based Wayland client does, e.g. Electron apps). It only
+      // steers dmabuf feedback; drawing ignores it. It must not crash Ash.
 
       if (state_.buffer.has_value() && state_.buffer->buffer() &&
           ShouldDisableOverlay(state_.buffer->buffer()->GetFormat())) {
